amonite-welcome (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Say what the system is: the handbook now covers the reasoning behind the
    defaults, the edition this installation runs, making the system yours,
    keeping it secure, and what to include when reporting a problem.
  * Read the edition from the VARIANT keys of os-release: it names the edition
    in the Welcome chapter and is listed under Your System. A distribution
    that publishes a single edition shows neither.
  * Offer installing software as an action again, through the software-install
    capability, shown only where a provider for it exists.
  * Take the palette from the running desktop: surfaces, text, borders and the
    accent are read from the GTK theme and derived into semantic roles, with a
    conservative adjustment when a colour would not be readable.
  * Compose the handbook as a document: numbered chapters, one reading measure,
    prose without containers, a dense fact table, and the chapter's actions as
    buttons below the text, with the recommended one marked.
  * Split the interface into shell, navigation, page view, components,
    accessibility and action activation; move platform code under
    amonite_welcome/services.
  * Key navigation on stable page ids instead of translated titles.
  * Let a distribution restyle Welcome with one file, theme/distro.css.
  * Keep capability visibility, accessibility semantics, keyboard navigation,
    the seven handbook languages, and the launcher options unchanged.

 -- Manuel Gil <security@amonite.org>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000

amonite-welcome (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show actions only when their capabilities are available.
  * Add --help, --version, and --capabilities to the launcher.
  * Fix terminal updates through the alternatives-selected terminal.
  * Remove the unsupported graphical package-manager action.
  * Fix accessible heading roles.
  * Align provider and packaging metadata with the installed system.

 -- Manuel Gil <security@amonite.org>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 23:55:00 +0000

